    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0906" n="792" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/411: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-21T17:00:00-05:45">January 21, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:39 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>17. My telegram No. 15, January 16, 5 p.m.<anchor n="14b" xml:id="d650-f1"/> The
                    boundary protocol was signed this afternoon. Its text will not be made public
                    here until after it has been submitted to Congress for ratification.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
